        <briefdescription>
<para>Applies a cell permutation to a mesh. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Cell-associated mesh data is reordered according to <computeroutput>permutation</computeroutput>, while cell indices stored in mesh connectivity are remapped to their corresponding new indices.</para>
<para>In particular, cell-associated data is reordered by position, whereas face owner and neighbour indices are remapped by value.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>mesh</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Mesh whose cell-related data is to be reordered. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>permutation</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="classNeoFOAM_1_1Permutation" kindref="compound">Permutation</ref> defining the mapping from old cell indices to new cell indices.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>permutation</computeroutput> is a valid permutation over the cells of <computeroutput>mesh</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>Cell-associated mesh data and cell references are consistent with the new cell ordering. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
